const intro={"n":10,"title":"Sergeant Cruz Remembers Love, Betrayal and Violence","summary":"The speaking voice changes: Sergeant Cruz addresses Fierro and recounts how he survived hardship through wit and stubbornness. He recalls a woman he loved and a commander who used his authority to intrude on their relationship and send Cruz away on errands. Finding the commander embracing her, Cruz confronts him and avoids killing the older officer, but kills another man who shoots at him. He leaves his home and turns toward life as a fugitive. The canto is Cruz's narrated history; readers should distinguish his account of events from his sweeping, disparaging remarks about women.","people":"Sergeant Cruz as the narrator of his own past; a woman he loved; the militia commander; an armed supporter of the commander whom Cruz kills.","themes":"The shift in speaking voice; exploitation of military rank; jealousy and gender prejudice; violence and accountability; the origins of Cruz's outlaw life.","words":"comendante (gauchesque form of comandante, commander); chasque (messenger or errand); poncho (woven cloak); facón (large rural knife); matrero (fugitive or outlaw).","questions":["How do we know Cruz, rather than Fierro, is narrating this story?","Which actions does Cruz attribute to the commander's military authority?","What happens to the officer, and whom does Cruz kill? Keep the two men distinct.","How does Cruz's pain become a generalized accusation against women, and why should readers question that conclusion?","How does his past help explain the solidarity he shows Fierro?"],"nums":[291,311,317],"analysis":"The narrative change matters. The commander is not killed in the confrontation: Cruz strikes him, then another armed man fires at Cruz and is killed. Cruz blames a woman's infidelity at the end, but the account also exposes a superior's abuse of position and Cruz's violent choices. The reader can understand his sense of betrayal without endorsing his sexist generalizations.","related":"/en/characters/","relatedTitle":"Characters: Cruz and the other figures"};
